request.description:
Assign a serviceman to a booking. Creates a `booking_assignment` record with status `assigned` and updates the booking's `service_man_id`.\n\n**Auth:** Bearer token (Console admin with `console.booking.assign` permission)\n\n**Path Parameters:**\n- `booking_id` — The booking ID\n\n**Body (form-data):**\n- `service_man_id` (required) — The user ID of the serviceman to assign\n\n**Validations:**\n- Booking must have `booking_status = booked` (not pending, completed, or cancelled)\n- Booking must not have an active assignment (assigned/accepted/on_way/in_progress)\n- Serviceman must be eligible: verified, active, same zone, matching category\n- `service_man_id` must exist in the users table\n\n**Response (200):**\n`json
{
 "status": true,
 "message": "Serviceman assigned successfully"
}
`\n\n**Error Examples:**\n- `400` — "Only booked orders can be assigned to a serviceman"\n- `400` — "This booking already has an active assignment"\n- `400` — "Serviceman is not eligible for this booking"\n- `422` — Validation errors for missing/invalid `service_man_id`\n\n**Note:** This replaces the old `GET /booking/update-service-man/{bookingId}/{userId}` endpoint. After assignment, the serviceman will see this as a pending request in their app.

Assign a serviceman to a booking. Creates a `booking_assignment` record with status `assigned` and updates the booking's `service_man_id`.\n\n**Auth:** Bearer token (Console admin with `console.booking.assign` permission)\n\n**Path Parameters:**\n- `booking_id` — The booking ID\n\n**Body (form-data):**\n- `service_man_id` (required) — The user ID of the serviceman to assign\n\n**Validations:**\n- Booking must have `booking_status = booked` (not pending, completed, or cancelled)\n- Booking must not have an active assignment (assigned/accepted/on_way/in_progress)\n- Serviceman must be eligible: verified, active, same zone, matching category\n- `service_man_id` must exist in the users table\n\n**Response (200):**\n`json
{
 "status": true,
 "message": "Serviceman assigned successfully"
}
`\n\n**Error Examples:**\n- `400` — "Only booked orders can be assigned to a serviceman"\n- `400` — "This booking already has an active assignment"\n- `400` — "Serviceman is not eligible for this booking"\n- `422` — Validation errors for missing/invalid `service_man_id`\n\n**Note:** This replaces the old `GET /booking/update-service-man/{bookingId}/{userId}` endpoint. After assignment, the serviceman will see this as a pending request in their app.

